{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d0ab0e42f795c99e75971caba10d92e7c022da7e02aeeb1d37a9daf0ff1419fc","digest":{"component_or_area":"module-size enforcement gate and contract","key_entities":[".github/module-size-allowlist.txt",".github/module-size-ceilings.txt","tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py","gerrit-verify.yaml","test.yml","docs/architecture.md",".github/module-size-limit.txt","src/rebar/**/*.py"],"problem_keywords":["module-size limit","allowlist","grandfathering","code organization","LOC cap","escape hatch"],"propositions":["The module-size allowlist (.github/module-size-allowlist.txt) and ceilings mechanism (.github/module-size-ceilings.txt) currently exempt 12 grandfathered modules from the 800 LOC soft cap, allowing them to persist and grow beyond the stated limit.","All 12 grandfathered modules must be split along call-graph seams and graduated off both the allowlist and ceilings files, with each split landing as a separate Gerrit change.","The allowlist and ceilings escape-hatch mechanism must be completely removed, replaced with an absolute 800 LOC hard cap test that rejects any over-cap file.","The 800 LOC module-size limit itself must be locked behind an admin-only gate (non-modifiable through normal contribution process) to prevent future casual increases."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787745361847930001,"uuid":"1c6a9876-c496-4deb-8337-22da3860086f"}